You’ve just found out that the last index of your list is 1, and the last member is 20, your ArrayList is filled with 4 integers. 
Your contract testing is not just about ensuring your array list is functioning correctly. It helps you understand how your code is operating, making bug hunting a smoother endeavour. And it's all about making sure that the contract is preserved. If you keep adding/removing/changing list members, and checking after every action, without breaking any contracts, you will ensure that your ArrayList is always working in the way you expect.
Another good practice you should adopt is to include tests to your code base, this will help ensure that the stability of your code throughout updates or in case of any future expansion.
Hope this helps you understand the role coverage plays in the context of ArrayList methods in Unit Testing.
If you have further inquiries, please feel free to ask.
Happy Learning & Have Fun Testing!!!
     

